<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling> a pk:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) & Erlich et al. (2016) mollusc shell marginal buckling, hollow-spine closure and predator damage / mantle repair (Pecten jacobaeus (Mediterranean scallop / Bivalvia, Ammonitida & Brachiopoda); Murex hollow spines (Gastropoda))",
        "Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) & Erlich et al. (2016) mollusc shell marginal buckling, hollow-spine closure and predator damage / mantle repair faithfully reproduces Pecten jacobaeus (Mediterranean scallop / Bivalvia, Ammonitida & Brachiopoda); Murex hollow spines (Gastropoda) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Pecten jacobaeus (Mediterranean scallop / Bivalvia, Ammonitida & Brachiopoda); Murex hollow spines (Gastropoda) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 87.0/100, audit 2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py> ;
    schema:about "Pecten jacobaeus (Mediterranean scallop / Bivalvia, Ammonitida & Brachiopoda); Murex hollow spines (Gastropoda)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A 3D finite-strain morphoelastic shell finite-element solution (Rudraraju et al. 2019), emergent spine base width or wall thickness, measured repair-callus mechanics, free-edge (non-periodic) margin boundary conditions, or an independent empirical closure strain for Murex spines",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Spectral L-BFGS-B minimisation of the fourth-order nonlinear Winkler-beam energy on a periodic margin (Pass 2), now with heterogeneous foundation k(s) and template-memory warm start; pitchfork amplitude law and subcritical control; 3D accretionary valve synthesis across 4 regimes; 12-species quarter-power regression; Pecten specimen costae segmentation; (Pass 3) planar inextensible elastica cross-section of a hollow spine fold with self-contact penalty, continuation in growth excess eps, and stacking into a tube surface; (Pass 3) 14-station damage/repair accretionary trajectory, scar index, healing-length fit, registry error, 5 x 4 chip-size x callus-stiffness outcome phase diagram",
        "reported_in_source: Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013): the mantle margin is an elastic beam on the Winkler foundation of the calcified shell edge; compressive growth thrust P above P_c = 2 sqrt(EI k) buckles it at lambda_c = 2 pi (EI/k)^(1/4), and hollow spines form where the buckled fold grows faster than its base",
        "reported_in_source: Erlich et al. (2016): isometric vs rib-intercalating antimarginal ornamentation follows from whether lambda_c scales with the margin length (constant N) or stays fixed (N grows)",
        "reported_in_source: Rudraraju et al. (2019): a 3D finite-strain morphoelastic shell FEM with surface and volume growth reproduces spine formation and closure",
        "reported_in_source: Vermeij (1987): durophagous predators chip shell margins; molluscs repair the break and leave repair scars",
        "transfer_boundary: EI = 1.085 mN mm^2 for Pecten is the value that makes lambda_c = 8.7766 mm give exactly 14 ribs over L = 122.87 mm; the vendored JSON default_parameters.EI_mN_mm2 is 0.18 and the Adult_V ontogenetic stage is 1.79, so the wild-type calibration is self-referential",
        "transfer_boundary: The hollow-spine closure model is a 2D cross-section elastica with prescribed base width W = 6 mm and wall thickness t = 0.35 mm; there is no out-of-plane coupling between cross-sections, no shell stretching energy and no growth tensor, so eps_close = 4.81 is a reduced-model number and its reference value (5.00) is mesh convergence of the same model, not a Murex measurement",
        "transfer_boundary: The repair callus stiffness ratio rho = 1.15 and decay length l_heal = 7 mm are prescribed, not measured; the critical chip arc 1.97 lambda is compared with a half-integer rounding heuristic (1.5 lambda), not a published repair-scar statistic" ;
    pk:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py; output: docs/media/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling_comparison.png; organism: Pecten jacobaeus (Mediterranean scallop / Bivalvia, Ammonitida & Brachiopoda); Murex hollow spines (Gastropoda); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/e651a8b8; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1; spec_fingerprint: 5ce4d2a0cdd2530a2bb4e03307b8a1565e305db6cf6b377ff8cb6db26ef82d9e; artifact_sha256: 9a3f32d98065e16f7fa63f39ab8a2b61e070b482616d8e3ef280efaef20643a0; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling_reference.json=dec7d148f176932a..., datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/pass3_spine_closure_damage_repair_reference.json=dcc719fadd231691..., datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/ribbed_bivalve_shell_specimen.jpg=a0ac69e8a9be3928..., datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/scout_manifest.json=2fb38cc60b112598...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013): the mantle margin is an elastic beam on the Winkler foundation of the calcified shell edge; compressive growth thrust P above P_c = 2 sqrt(EI k) buckles it at lambda_c = 2 pi (EI/k)^(1/4), and hollow spines form where the buckled fold grows faster than its base | Erlich et al. (2016): isometric vs rib-intercalating antimarginal ornamentation follows from whether lambda_c scales with the margin length (constant N) or stays fixed (N grows) | Rudraraju et al. (2019): a 3D finite-strain morphoelastic shell FEM with surface and volume growth reproduces spine formation and closure | Vermeij (1987): durophagous predators chip shell margins; molluscs repair the break and leave repair scars; reconstructed_in_script: Spectral L-BFGS-B minimisation of the fourth-order nonlinear Winkler-beam energy on a periodic margin (Pass 2), now with heterogeneous foundation k(s) and template-memory warm start; pitchfork amplitude law and subcritical control; 3D accretionary valve synthesis across 4 regimes; 12-species quarter-power regression; Pecten specimen costae segmentation; (Pass 3) planar inextensible elastica cross-section of a hollow spine fold with self-contact penalty, continuation in growth excess eps, and stacking into a tube surface; (Pass 3) 14-station damage/repair accretionary trajectory, scar index, healing-length fit, registry error, 5 x 4 chip-size x callus-stiffness outcome phase diagram; transfer_boundary: The hollow-spine closure model is a 2D cross-section elastica with prescribed base width W = 6 mm and wall thickness t = 0.35 mm; there is no out-of-plane coupling between cross-sections, no shell stretching energy and no growth tensor, so eps_close = 4.81 is a reduced-model number and its reference value (5.00) is mesh convergence of the same model, not a Murex measurement | The repair callus stiffness ratio rho = 1.15 and decay length l_heal = 7 mm are prescribed, not measured; the critical chip arc 1.97 lambda is compared with a half-integer rounding heuristic (1.5 lambda), not a published repair-scar statistic | EI = 1.085 mN mm^2 for Pecten is the value that makes lambda_c = 8.7766 mm give exactly 14 ribs over L = 122.87 mm; the vendored JSON default_parameters.EI_mN_mm2 is 0.18 and the Adult_V ontogenetic stage is 1.79, so the wild-type calibration is self-referential; does_not_claim: A 3D finite-strain morphoelastic shell finite-element solution (Rudraraju et al. 2019), emergent spine base width or wall thickness, measured repair-callus mechanics, free-edge (non-periodic) margin boundary conditions, or an independent empirical closure strain for Murex spines]; other sources: Evolution and Escalation: An Ecological History of Life <https://press.princeton.edu/books/paperback/9780691000800/evolution-and-escalation>" ;
    pk:derivedFromPaper <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jtbi.2012.07.009>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.1220443110>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1098/rsif.2016.0592>,
