<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) & Erlich et al. (2016) mollusc shell marginal buckling, hollow-spine closure and predator damage / mantle repair — Code-to-model traceability: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The header docstring (L1-78) maps Laws 1-5 to Chirat et al. (2013) PNAS, Erlich et al. (2016), Rudraraju et al. (2019) and the 7 Lean theorems by name, and states plainly that Law 5 is an honest reduced stand-in for the 3D FEM (L74-77); the Pass 3 functions carry docstrings tying k(s) to the callus theorem (L244-252) and the elastica energy to its terms (L524-531); the math-KG YAML registers the two new laws with single-range `code_locus` pins refreshed to current lines. Deductions: the `--self-test` help string still says \"Run 8-check verification suite\" although 12 checks run (L2343) (-2); the section banner at L1265 still says \"6-Panel Synthesis Figure\" for a 3 x 3 figure (-1); the hard-coded 1.085 / 0.285 / 1.250 constants in `measure_morphoeval` (L2039, L2042) are not traced to the JSON (-2); `mu_end = mu_contact = 400` penalties are chosen without a cited rationale (L517-519) (-2); the heuristic reference values are labelled as such in `reference_source` strings, which is credited (-3 net total)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py L2036–L2043: measure_morphoeval hard-codes L=122.87, EI=1.085, k=0.285, kappa_3=1.250 rather than reading the pinned JSON <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py#L2036-L2043>",
        "2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py L2343–L2343: Stale CLI help: 'Run 8-check verification suite' while self_test() runs 12 checks <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py#L2343-L2343>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-code-traceability-2> ;
    pk:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) & Erlich et al. (2016) mollusc shell marginal buckling, hollow-spine closure and predator damage / mantle repair — Model fidelity to source: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The Pass 2 core is intact: exact fourth-order nonlinear Winkler-beam energy minimised by spectral L-BFGS-B (`relax_winkler_mantle_margin`, L221-359) with P_c = 2 sqrt(EI k), lambda_c = 2 pi (EI/k)^(1/4) and the supercritical pitchfork law (L164-202). Pass 3 adds a physically honest reduced model of spine closure — an inextensible planar elastica with clamped roots, end penalty and pairwise self-contact penalty, continuation in eps, and the small-strain amplitude law A = (2/pi) sqrt(W dL) recovered to r = 0.99999 (L511-729) — and a heterogeneous-foundation extension with template memory that keeps the default path bitwise identical (L244-252, L292-298). Deductions: the requested 3D finite-strain morphoelastic FEM was not built; the elastica has no out-of-plane coupling, stretching energy or growth tensor, and W, t are prescribed (-4); the solver never converges to its ftol = 1e-16 / gtol = 1e-13 tolerances and always exits at maxiter (L310, L357), so the \"equilibria\" are iteration-count-limited (-3); the periodic FFT margin on [0, L) is applied to an open valve fan, which makes an intercalated rib slide the whole pattern (L234, L263, L328) (-2); the `antimarginal_intercalating_multicostate` and `cancellate_spiny_episodic_varix` rib fields are prescribed cosines rather than solver output and `n_ribs_adult = 2 n_base - 0.5` is hard-coded (L364-459, L435) (-3); EI = 1.085 is back-fitted to the rib count rather than derived from mantle mechanics (L224, L473) (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py L364–L459: 3D accretionary synthesis; intercalating and varix regimes are prescribed cosine fields and n_ribs_adult = 2*n_base - 0.5 is hard-coded at L435, not solver output <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py#L364-L459>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-model-fidelity-5> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.6e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) & Erlich et al. (2016) mollusc shell marginal buckling, hollow-spine closure and predator damage / mantle repair — Morphometric validation: 83/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L2036-2222) now returns 16 measurements with reference values: the 9 Pass 2 metrics are unchanged (lambda_sim 8.7728 vs 8.7766 mm, pitchfork r 0.9992, specimen 14 costae, CV 0.2196) and 7 are new (small-strain r = 1.0, eps_close 4.8068, gap/t 0.9997, adult N 14, scar index 0.030, local P_c ratio sqrt(rho) 1.0724, critical chip 1.97 lambda). Deductions, which drive this dimension down from 92: the three headline Pass 3 references are not independent data — eps_close is compared with mesh convergence of the same model at M = 224 (L2069-2079), the critical chip with a rounding heuristic (L2119-2129), and the heal-length fit 8.3 mm with the imposed 7 mm (consistency check, L2089-2110) (-5); the 12-species quarter-power \"collapse\" regresses lambda_obs against 2 pi (EI/k)^(1/4) where the JSON EI, k were themselves set from lambda_obs, so r = 1.0000 and alpha = 0.2500 are tautological (L1073-1139) (-3); the rib-count ratio 27.5/14 compares the hard-coded `2 n_base - 0.5` with its own reference (L435) (-1); the rib count in the damage trajectory depends on a `find_peaks` prominence threshold of 0.25 A_eq (L836), so the sector count 1 -> 0 at damage is threshold-dependent (-1); the registry/defect metrics inherit the periodic-margin artefact (adult correlation ~ 0 in defect cells) (-1)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py L1073–L1139: 12-species regression of lambda_obs on 2 pi (EI/k)^(1/4) with EI, k read from the JSON that was fitted to lambda_obs — tautological r = 1.0000 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py#L1073-L1139>",
        "2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py L2069–L2079: eps_close reference is the same model's mesh-convergence value at M = 224, stated as such — not an empirical closure strain <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py#L2069-L2079>",
        "2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py L2119–L2129: Critical chip reference is a half-integer rounding heuristic (1.5 lambda), stated as such; numeric value 1.97 lambda <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py#L2119-L2129>",
        "2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py L829–L840: Rib crest count via find_peaks with prominence 0.25 A_eq (L836) — threshold-dependent <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py#L829-L840>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-measurement-12-species-antimarginal-rib-wavelength-scaling-correlation-chirat-et-al-2013-erlich-et-al-2016>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-measurement-12-species-rib-count-scaling-correlation-n-ribs-phi-0-r-lambda-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-measurement-adult-rib-count-after-predator-chip-and-mantle-repair-default-chip-5-deg-half-angle-rho-1-15>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-measurement-biological-specimen-polar-angular-rib-spacing-cv-ribbed-bivalve-shell-specimen-jpg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-measurement-biological-specimen-segmented-primary-radial-costae-count-ribbed-bivalve-shell-specimen-jpg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-measurement-critical-predator-chip-arc-in-lambda-c-for-repair-induced-rib-intercalation-at-rho-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-measurement-hollow-spine-elastica-small-strain-amplitude-law-correlation-a-num-vs-2-pi-sqrt-w-dl>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-measurement-hollow-spine-neck-gap-wall-thickness-after-self-contact-contact-penalty-resolution>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-measurement-hollow-spine-self-contact-closure-growth-excess-eps-close-reduced-2d-elastica-of-a-murex-spine-fold>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-measurement-intercalating-multicostate-vs-isometric-constant-rib-adult-count-ratio>,
