<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Chirat, Moulton & Goriely (2013) & Erlich et al. (2016) mollusc shell marginal buckling, hollow-spine closure and predator damage / mantle repair — Morphological realism / specimen match: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The SHA-256-locked *Pecten jacobaeus* valve is still segmented to all 14 primary costae (`segment_pecten_specimen`, L1181-1265; dtheta = 9.40 deg, CV = 0.2196), and the Pass 3 3 x 3 synthesis figure plus the new 3D figure and 14-frame GIF render a recognisable hollow spine fold closing into a tube and a chipped valve healing back into register (L1267-1785, L1896-2033). Deductions: no Murex specimen is vendored, so the spine geometry (W = 6 mm, t = 0.35 mm, H/W at closure 2.31) is compared with nothing (-5); no repair-scar specimen or image is vendored, so the damage/repair trajectory is validated only against its own control (-4); the damaged-valve surface below the first station is a presentation-only linear amplitude ramp (L1051-1057) (-1); the Pecten segmentation uses a fixed `find_peaks` prominence/distance (L1232) tuned to this one image (-1); panel titles A/B/C overlap slightly in the 3 x 3 layout (pre-existing) (-1); the Pass 2 image evidence remains valid." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py L1037–L1070: build_damaged_valve_surface: chip notch for the figure; inner region below first station is a linear ramp (L1051-1057), presentation only <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/2013-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling.py#L1037-L1070>",
        "datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/README.md L1–L40: Only one specimen (Pecten jacobaeus valve) is vendored; no Murex spine or repair-scar specimen <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e651a8b8/datasets/mollusc_shell_marginal_buckling/README.md#L1-L40>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-chirat-mollusc-shell-marginal-buckling-specimen-match-2>,
